
Moving to use the VALOR framework rather than a standalone analysis package entailed a number of changes, which will mean the macros will generally need to be updated.

A (probably incomplete) list of changes that need to be made

namespace t2kana->valor (find and replace)
FitParameterList::NamedParameterList -> util::NamedParameterList
FitInputs::Chisquare => FitInputs::Statistic
FitInputs::BestFitChisquare => FitParamList => BestFitStatistic 

Skobs/Skexp's GetSpectrum (histogram) methods now allocate a new histogram, which should be deleted or it'll leak memory over time (if you call skobs->GetCurrErecoHist()->Integral() for example)

After setting analysis options in Opt() like dmsq scheme and mixing param choice, you should  then call Opt::Instance()->SetDefaultParameters()

Opt::gOscAnaType now lives in T2KOpt


